From: Marmalade STT <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Whisper features: kissfft instead of a naive DFT; reuse the FFT plan (#53)

Not upstream; ours. WhisperFeatureComputer (the log-mel front-end of
Whisper and Qwen3-ASR in sherpa-onnx) used whisper.cpp's recursive radix-2
FFT. For the 400-point frame it halves 400 -> 200 -> 100 -> 50 -> 25 and then
runs a naive DFT with a sin and a cos per term: 14.4 ms of one core per
second of audio on the benchmark host (Ryzen AI Max+ 395), 8-15 % of Qwen3-ASR's
decode time. It now uses knf's own Rfft (kissfft, mixed radix): 0.16 ms.
The features differ only by float rounding: at most 5.2e-4 after Whisper's
normalisation, whose range is 2.0.

Rfft also allocated its kissfft plan (malloc plus twiddle factors) on every
frame. The plan is now made once per Rfft. That speeds up the Kaldi fbank
(Parakeet, Canary, Nemotron) 2.8x and leaves its output bit-identical.

The naive DFT is still in v1.22.3 (the latest release) and on master
as of 2026-10-02.
---
--- a/kaldi-native-fbank/csrc/rfft.cc
+++ b/kaldi-native-fbank/csrc/rfft.cc
@@ -39,8 +39,17 @@
       fprintf(stderr, "n should be positive. Given: %d \n", n);
       exit(-1);
     }
+
+    // Marmalade STT (#53): allocated once, not per frame. kiss_fftr_alloc()
+    // mallocs and computes the twiddle factors.
+    cfg_ = kiss_fftr_alloc(n_, inverse_, nullptr, nullptr);
   }
 
+  ~RfftImpl() { kiss_fftr_free(cfg_); }
+
+  RfftImpl(const RfftImpl &) = delete;
+  RfftImpl &operator=(const RfftImpl &) = delete;
+
   void Compute(float *in_out) {
     if (!inverse_) {
       Forward(in_out);
@@ -59,13 +68,9 @@
 
  private:
   void Forward(float *in_out) const {
-    kiss_fftr_cfg cfg = kiss_fftr_alloc(n_, 0, nullptr, nullptr);
-
     std::vector<kiss_fft_cpx> out(n_ / 2 + 1);
 
-    kiss_fftr(cfg, in_out, out.data());
-
-    kiss_fftr_free(cfg);
+    kiss_fftr(cfg_, in_out, out.data());
 
     in_out[0] = out[0].r;
     in_out[1] = out[n_ / 2].r;
@@ -89,16 +94,13 @@
       out[i].i = in_out[2 * i + 1];
     }
 
-    kiss_fftr_cfg cfg = kiss_fftr_alloc(n_, 1, nullptr, nullptr);
-
-    kiss_fftri(cfg, out.data(), in_out);
-
-    kiss_fftr_free(cfg);
+    kiss_fftri(cfg_, out.data(), in_out);
   }
 
  private:
   int32_t n_;
   bool inverse_ = false;
+  kiss_fftr_cfg cfg_ = nullptr;
 };
 
 Rfft::Rfft(int32_t n, bool inverse /*=false*/)
